From 0d7c2a498c6e4e1d4b327762a785f4cb17e064fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:34:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] software_isp: debayer_egl: Smooth the chroma

At high gain the picture carries blotchy colour noise, coarser than
the 3x3 luma filter of the second pass and untouched by it.

Average the colour differences over a 9x9 footprint (16 taps at 2 and
4 pixels in eight directions) in the same pass, weighted by luma and
chroma similarity so that colour doesn't bleed across edges and real
colour detail survives, and rebuild RGB from the filtered luma and the
smoothed chroma. The Detail algorithm drives it from the tuning file's
chromaDenoise, scaled with the square root of the gain like the luma
smoothing; 0.03 for the four Pixel 7 Pro cameras.

On a synthetic chart with high-gain noise, the shader's numpy port
cuts the chroma noise on flat patches from 6.1 to 2.8 (gain 4) and from
12.1 to 5.6 (gain 16), 8-bit RMS, and changes a clean picture's colour
at edges and 6 px colour stripes by 1.0 and 1.9.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
